**JVM flags:** queries go through Arrow Flight, which needs:
- `--add-opens=java.base/java.nio=ALL-UNNAMED` on JDK 17 and later.
- `--sun-misc-unsafe-memory-access=allow` only on newer JDKs that restrict `sun.misc.Unsafe`. JDKs before 23 won't start with this flag.

If you run with `mvn exec:java`, put these in `MAVEN_OPTS`.

## 3. Service code

```java
package com.example.influx;

import com.influxdb.v3.client.InfluxDBClient;
import com.influxdb.v3.client.Point;
import com.influxdb.v3.client.query.QueryOptions;
import com.influxdb.v3.client.query.QueryType;
import io.github.cdimascio.dotenv.Dotenv;

import java.net.URI;
import java.net.http.HttpClient;
import java.net.http.HttpRequest;
import java.net.http.HttpResponse;
import java.time.Duration;
import java.time.Instant;
import java.util.List;
import java.util.Map;
import java.util.stream.Stream;

public final class InfluxService implements AutoCloseable {

    private final InfluxDBClient client;
    private final String database;

    public InfluxService() {
        Dotenv env = Dotenv.configure().ignoreIfMissing().load();
        String host = require(env, "INFLUXDB_HOST");
        String token = require(env, "INFLUXDB_TOKEN");
        this.database = require(env, "INFLUXDB_DATABASE");

        // Stop at startup if the database is missing. Enterprise silently
        // auto-creates a database on the first write, so a typo in
        // INFLUXDB_DATABASE would otherwise send data to a new, wrong database.
        verifyDatabaseExists(host, token, database);

        this.client = InfluxDBClient.getInstance(host, token.toCharArray(), database);
    }

    public void writeBatch(List<Point> points) {
        // Batch 1,000+ points or flush every second, whichever comes first.
        client.writePoints(points);
    }

    public Stream<Object[]> readingsForHost(String hostTag) {
        // Pass user input as a parameter; never concatenate it into the SQL.
        QueryOptions opts = new QueryOptions(database, QueryType.SQL)
            .withParameters(Map.of("host", hostTag));   // adjust to your client version's API
        return client.query(
            "SELECT time, temperature, humidity FROM sensor " +
            "WHERE host = $host AND time >= now() - INTERVAL '1 hour' " +
            "ORDER BY time DESC LIMIT 100",
            opts);
    }

    public static Point reading(String host, String region, double temp, double humidity) {
        return Point.measurement("sensor")
            .setTag("host", host)          // identifies the source, so it's a tag
            .setTag("region", region)
            .setFloatField("temperature", temp)
            .setFloatField("humidity", humidity)
            .setTimestamp(Instant.now());
    }

    private static void verifyDatabaseExists(String host, String token, String db) {
        HttpRequest req = HttpRequest.newBuilder()
            .uri(URI.create(host.replaceAll("/+$", "") + "/api/v3/configure/database?format=json"))
            .header("Authorization", "Bearer " + token)
            .timeout(Duration.ofSeconds(10))
            .GET().build();
        try {
            HttpResponse<String> resp = HttpClient.newHttpClient()
                .send(req, HttpResponse.BodyHandlers.ofString());
            switch (resp.statusCode()) {
                case 200 -> {
                    if (!resp.body().contains("\"" + db + "\"")) {
                        throw new IllegalStateException(
                            "Database '" + db + "' does not exist. Create it with " +
                            "`influxdb3 create database " + db + "` before starting the service.");
                    }
                }
                case 401 -> throw new IllegalStateException(
                    "INFLUXDB_TOKEN was rejected (401). Check the token value.");
                case 403 -> verifyByQuery(host, token, db); // scoped token can't list databases
                default -> throw new IllegalStateException(
                    "Unexpected " + resp.statusCode() + " checking databases at " + host);
            }
        } catch (java.io.IOException | InterruptedException e) {
            throw new IllegalStateException("Cannot reach InfluxDB at " + host, e);
        }
    }

    // Fallback for tokens without admin rights: a read against a missing
    // database fails instead of auto-creating it.
    private static void verifyByQuery(String host, String token, String db) {
        try (InfluxDBClient probe = InfluxDBClient.getInstance(host, token.toCharArray(), db);
             Stream<Object[]> rows = probe.query("SELECT table_name FROM information_schema.tables LIMIT 1")) {
            rows.count();
        } catch (Exception e) {
            throw new IllegalStateException(
                "Database '" + db + "' is missing or this token can't read it: " + e.getMessage(), e);
        }
    }

    private static String require(Dotenv env, String key) {
        String v = env.get(key);   // dotenv-java also falls back to real env vars
        if (v == null || v.isBlank()) throw new IllegalStateException("Missing env var " + key);
        return v;
    }

    @Override
    public void close() throws Exception {
        client.close();
    }
}
```

Create one `InfluxService` when the service starts, share it everywhere (the client is thread-safe), and close it on shutdown.

## Things to know

- **Startup database check:** the code first tries to list databases. A token scoped to only read and write one database may get a 403 there. In that case it falls back to a read query, which should fail on a missing database rather than create it. The docs don't confirm either of those two behaviors, so test once with a misspelled `INFLUXDB_DATABASE`: the service should refuse to start. If it starts anyway, create the database in your deploy pipeline instead of relying on the check.
- **One bad line rejects the whole batch:** client 1.10.0 and later sends writes to `/api/v2/write` by default. If you'd rather keep the valid lines, set the `useV2Api` write option to `false`.
- **Retries:** retry on 5xx and 429. Don't retry on 400, 401, 403 or 404; those need a fix, not a retry.
- **Timestamps:** use second precision unless a series can get more than one point per second. Points with the same table, tags and timestamp overwrite each other.
- **Tokens:** in production, set the three env vars from your secret manager and don't ship a `.env`. To rotate the token, create the new one, update the secret, and only then revoke the old one.
- **Queries:** use SQL; InfluxQL is only for v1/v2 compatibility.

