## Things to know

- **One bad line can reject a whole batch.** From version 1.9.0 the client writes to `/api/v2/write` by default, which rejects all 10,000 points if any line is invalid. On Core or Enterprise, you can set the client's `UseV2Api` write option to `false` to use `/api/v3/write_lp` instead. That endpoint stores the valid lines and returns 400 listing the rejected ones, so you resend only those. Keep the default for Cloud Serverless, Cloud Dedicated and Clustered.
- **Duplicate points overwrite each other.** A point with the same table, tags and timestamp as an existing one replaces it. With second precision, any series that gets more than one point per second needs a finer precision, such as `WritePrecision.Ms`.
- **Field types can't change.** `temperature` becomes a float on the first write, and a later string value for it will get a 400.
- **Tuning beyond this is out of scope here.** Batch sizes, concurrency and server-side ingest settings for your hardware are covered in the performance-tuning docs: https://docs.influxdata.com/influxdb3/core/admin/performance-tuning/. Start with 10,000 × 4 and change one setting at a time while watching the points-per-second output.

A 429 means the server is rate-limiting you. It's a temporary error, so **wait and resend the same batch**. Use exponential backoff with jitter, and don't drop the data.

## Why you're getting it

- **InfluxDB Cloud Serverless** limits writes per organization. This is the most likely cause.
- **Self-hosted Core or Enterprise** usually doesn't return 429 unless someone configured a limit, or a proxy or load balancer in front of it is doing the limiting.

## Retry in Go (`influxdb3-go`)

Resending the whole batch is safe. Points with the same table, tags and timestamp overwrite each other, so a retry won't create duplicates.

```go
import (
    "context"
    "errors"
    "math/rand"
    "net/http"
    "strconv"
    "time"

    "github.com/InfluxCommunity/influxdb3-go/v2/influxdb3"
)

func writeWithRetry(ctx context.Context, c *influxdb3.Client, points []*influxdb3.Point) error {
    const maxAttempts = 6
    backoff := 500 * time.Millisecond
    const maxBackoff = 30 * time.Second

    for attempt := 1; ; attempt++ {
        err := c.WritePoints(ctx, points)
        if err == nil {
            return nil
        }

        var se *influxdb3.ServerError
        if !errors.As(err, &se) || !retriable(se.StatusCode) || attempt == maxAttempts {
            return err // 400/401/403/404, or out of attempts: don't retry blindly
        }

        // Use the server's Retry-After header if it sent one; otherwise use backoff plus full jitter.
        wait := time.Duration(rand.Int63n(int64(backoff)))
        if ra := se.Headers.Get("Retry-After"); ra != "" {
            if secs, perr := strconv.Atoi(ra); perr == nil {
                wait = time.Duration(secs) * time.Second
            }
        }

        select {
        case <-time.After(wait):
        case <-ctx.Done():
            return ctx.Err()
        }
        backoff = min(backoff*2, maxBackoff)
    }
}

func retriable(code int) bool {
    return code == http.StatusTooManyRequests || code >= 500
}
