## If it keeps happening

- **Send fewer, larger requests.** Batch about 1,000 points per write or flush every 1 second, whichever comes first. Many tiny writes hit rate limits sooner than a few large ones.
- **Limit concurrency.** If several goroutines write at once, route them through one writer or a small worker pool so retries don't all fire together.
- **Don't retry non-retriable errors.** Retry only 429 and 5xx. A 400, 401, 403 or 404 needs a code or config fix.
- **On Cloud Serverless,** if you hit the limit even with reasonable batching, check your plan's write limits in the Serverless docs. Changing your code won't raise the limit.

